WEBVTT

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:49.990
This is Lakeview, California, one of a score of American communities which came into being during and after World War II.

00:01:50.680 --> 00:02:00.000
This is the Lakeview Research Laboratory of Nuclear Physics, one of the top secret government projects vital to the national defense and security.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.290
To be a worker at Lakeview, one must be first, an American of proven loyalty.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:13.490
The task of guarding projects like Lakeview is entrusted to the Federal Bureau of Investigation,

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:17.830
which explains why Special Agent Daniel F. O'Hara, in charge of the Lakeview security

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:22.530
detail, remains in his office long after regular hours, night after night.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:37.200
- Hi. - Oh, what are you doing here this time of night?

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.870
- Trying to win the Legion of Merit? - Just refreshing my memory.

00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:43.200
Waiting for a phone call from Jimmy Colton.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:45.110
He's out at Lakeview on a deal.

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:49.450
- What are you doing here on your time? - Pre-checking last week's applications for employment at Lakeview.

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:56.330
- About 300 of them. - Oh, Harold.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.040
Dan, this is Colton.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.780
I'm talking from a booth at the Lakeview Arena.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:05.960
I think I've run into something red-hot.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:08.000
You mean something connected with Radchik?

00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:10.700
Yeah, that's right. Can you get over here right away?

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.610
- 20 minutes. - That'll be...

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:23.330
Jimmy! Jimmy! Jimmy!

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.660
Whoever gave it to him sure got away clean.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.570
All the excitement and yelling inside, nobody even heard the shots.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:54.890
This young lady just happened to pass by the booth and glance inside.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:55.890
It looks funny to her.

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:59.110
So she opens the door, lets Holly out, and planes set away.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:00.000
He was...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.330
I thought he was tight or asleep, and then I saw...

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:08.360
- You didn't see who did it? - No, no. I only saw him. Just like that.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:11.120
I phoned in the report. The Homicide Squad should be here any minute.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.510
Tried to identify him. Didn't have anything on him.

00:04:13.570 --> 00:04:19.680
His name is James Colton. He lived at 110 F Street here in Lakeview.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:25.040
That's about all we can do here. Sergeant, will you...

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:26.500
- I'll take care of everything. - Right.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.000
I can't understand why anyone would want to kill a fine...

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.750
All right, folks, that's it. Break it up.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.490
Come on, everybody move. Please, break it up, break it up.

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:36.690
You've got other places to go. Come on, what's the matter?

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:54.080
I'm sorry to bring you back to the office this time of night, Mr. North,

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:57.870
but I wanted your permission to follow this rad check thing through to a finish.

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.420
I understand how you feel, Dan.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.640
Colton was a fine boy.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:06.060
It must be demonstrated to Mr. Radchick, as it has been to others who have had the same idea...

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:11.120
...that the murder of an FBI man inevitably leads to very disagreeable consequences.

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:13.400
Radchick.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.960
I remember the name, but it was some time ago.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.410
About a year ago.

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:22.930
An order went out at that time to pick him up on suspicion of illegal entry into the country.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:25.480
Oh, yes. Now I remember.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:29.860
- He did a vanishing act before he could be brought in. - That's right.

00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:33.690
And he didn't show again until I spotted him day before yesterday.

00:05:34.530 --> 00:05:38.740
I'd picked him up then instead of putting Colton on him to find out what he was doing in Lakeview.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:40.950
Jimmy'd still be alive.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:43.030
People die of old age, too, dear.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:47.440
What could Colton have come up with to force Radcheck to take such a crazy chance?

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.900
Commit murder practically in front of a couple of thousand witnesses.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.780
I'll remember to ask Radcheck that when I meet him in person.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.430
- I've got all avenues out of Lakeview covered. - Good.

00:05:58.150 --> 00:05:59.890
By the way, Mr. North,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.400
Do you remember the... Excuse me.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:07.780
O'Hara, Allison, at the Lakeview bus depot.

00:06:07.780 --> 00:06:09.780
The subject just bought himself a ticket for San Francisco.

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:12.170
Good. Hang on to him.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:17.960
Allison, he's found Radcheck, Lakeview bus depot.

00:06:17.960 --> 00:06:18.860
Bring him in, then.

00:06:18.860 --> 00:06:20.890
Bring him in and then what?

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:22.890
Not a shred of evidence to connect him with Colton's death.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:23.890
Stay with him long enough.

00:06:23.890 --> 00:06:26.890
He'll probably win his confidence and get a confession.

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:29.280
Thanks, Mr. North.

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:38.530
Thirty minutes later, Anton Radchak boarded a bus at the Lakeview terminal.

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:55.140
O'Hara delayed arresting Radchak.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:07:00.000
He was certain that Radchak had not murdered Colton merely to escape a relatively mild

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:04.990
charge of illegal entry into the United States. Using Radshak to point out any

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:23.060
contacts he might have, O'Hara and Allison trailed him to San Francisco. As the bus

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:30.000
crossed the Big Bay Bridge, Radshak's sense of smug satisfaction increased. His growing sense of

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.620
security fell in with O'Hara's plan of action, which was to use Radchak as a bird dog to

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:40.900
lead them to whatever connections he had in San Francisco. Connections which might explain

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:48.050
the reason for Radchak's presence in Lakeview. At the bus terminal, Radchak took a taxi cab

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:52.870
and led O'Hara and Allison to a rooming house in an older section of the city.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:13.130
See you later.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:13.550
Right.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:26.560
Aided by the agents of the San Francisco office,

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:30.000
O'Hara set up a 24-hour surveillance of Rags

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:37.130
hideout. A motion picture camera was concealed in constantly changing vehicles, and everyone

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:53.000
who entered or left the rooming house was secretly photographed. The only telephone

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:58.790
in the house was monitored, and every incoming or outgoing call recorded by an agent, whose

00:08:58.790 --> 00:09:00.000
equipment was set up at the house.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.310
in a basement of a house on the next street.

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:05.740
But Radjack had no visitors,

00:09:05.740 --> 00:09:08.180
and left the house only to take his meals

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:10.810
and to buy a newspaper at the corner restaurant.

00:09:10.810 --> 00:09:11.650
- Thank you, sir.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.360
Evening papers.

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.780
Get the evening paper here.

00:09:15.780 --> 00:09:17.090
Evening paper.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:49.560
Right, Jack.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:20.730
- Gaines. Maybe I got something. - You're right over.

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:22.600
Right.

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.780
or a half a dozen bookies in O'Leary's Saloon down on the corner.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.320
Wait till I get my hands on him.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:36.950
That was Mrs. Green.

00:10:37.640 --> 00:10:40.420
We've been able to identify the voices of everybody in the house,

00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:41.600
but this is a new one.

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:43.430
It identifies itself.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:02.120
53 Octavia Street, second floor front.

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:05.760
- You'll take care of things, Igor? - Of course I'll take care of things.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:12.560
- Thank you. Good night. - That's what we want. Can you trace that call?

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.720
- And dial telephones. It's tough. - How long will it take?

00:11:15.790 --> 00:11:20.320
The miraculous we do immediately. The impossible takes a few minutes longer. Good boy.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:29.510
At 10:30 the next morning, O'Hara was summoned to Radshak's hideout by a telephone call from Allison.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:45.250
I don't know, maybe nothing. But I'm a little worried.

00:11:45.250 --> 00:11:47.710
Well, every morning he goes for breakfast at 8 o'clock, right?

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:48.710
Yeah.

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:51.710
Well, it's past 10:30 now, and he hasn't even shown. That's why I called you.

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:54.870
Oh, I see. No visitors?

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:55.720
Nobody in or out.

00:11:55.720 --> 00:11:59.210
Find out whether or not he's in that room.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.500
Pull a wire, Inspector Gaggin, see if he's there.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:15.520
- Don't buy that anymore. - And make sure you're home in time for dinner.

00:12:15.520 --> 00:12:16.580
Yeah, I'll be here.

00:12:50.190 --> 00:12:53.690
Say, Dan, I think you better come up.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:04.570
- What's happened? - Take a look.

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:11.050
That explains why he didn't get down to breakfast.

00:13:11.130 --> 00:13:15.360
Right through the heart, hardly any blood at all.

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:18.680
Rigor mortis is complete.

00:13:19.390 --> 00:13:20.800
He's probably been dead for hours.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:24.000
That means he was killed sometime last night.

00:13:36.810 --> 00:13:39.480
- No visitors, eh? - Well, I was on.

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.840
- Maybe he found out we had him boxed up and killed himself. - Uh-uh.

00:13:43.340 --> 00:13:46.100
This Los Angeles paper didn't walk in here by itself.

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:47.730
It's three days old.

00:13:48.020 --> 00:13:51.480
The fellow down at the corner where Radcheck got his news doesn't sell out of town sheets.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.590
That means that the killer brought it with him.

00:13:54.530 --> 00:13:57.080
He also brought that knife. He really came prepared.

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:59.860
I know, but a man with a knife, why didn't Radcheck call out?

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.820
Look at him. Position in the chair. Look at the room. No sign of a struggle.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:06.240
Whoever killed him, he trusted.

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:10.850
The way it looks, Mr. Radcheck suddenly became an embarrassment to his friends.

00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.800
It was just a little too hot to handle.

00:14:14.810 --> 00:14:17.050
I'm going back down to the office and take a look at that film we shot.

00:14:17.150 --> 00:14:19.410
- You stay here and call the police. - Right.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:25.320
In the San Francisco office of the FBI,

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:29.730
O'Hara called together all of the agents working with him on the Radcheck case.

00:14:30.030 --> 00:14:32.730
In a projection room, they studied every foot of the film

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:36.150
photographed by the hidden camera.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:40.110
That's Mrs. Green, lived there for five years.

00:14:40.570 --> 00:14:43.260
As you can see, she loves to talk.

00:14:45.010 --> 00:14:48.440
That's Mrs. Katz, landlady.

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:53.920
That's Albert Green, second floor rear.

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:57.750
Mrs. Green's husband, he never gets a chance to talk.

00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:04.600
- Mrs. Harner, first floor front. - And the milkman.

00:15:05.410 --> 00:15:08.670
He used to drop bombs, now he drops bottles.

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:13.170
That's old man Katz. Coming home with a snoot-pull.

00:15:17.740 --> 00:15:27.400
- What's his name? - Freeze it.

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:37.620
- Miller, you shot this last night? - That's right.

00:15:37.710 --> 00:15:39.930
- Who is this gentleman? - Well, you can see for yourself.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:42.720
- He's a clergyman. - What time did he go in?

00:15:43.470 --> 00:15:45.200
11:48.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:48.320
- You were covering the front end. Did you see him? - Yeah, sure.

00:15:48.520 --> 00:15:52.240
- Whom did he visit? - I don't know. He just came in and went upstairs.

00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:55.760
- Uh-huh. How long did he stay? - Not more than 15 minutes.

00:15:55.960 --> 00:15:58.870
He came back down at 2 minutes past 12.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.300
We know and have checked everyone that went in or out of that house

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:03.800
after the minute of Radcheck's murder.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:06.700
He's the only person that we don't know.

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:09.120
Therefore, he's your killer.

00:16:10.160 --> 00:16:11.420
But, Dan, a clergyman?

00:16:11.480 --> 00:16:13.800
Well, anybody can put on a black suit and turn his collar around.

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:14.420
Who followed him?

00:16:17.780 --> 00:16:18.520
Well, who followed him?

00:16:18.900 --> 00:16:22.890
Well, I guess I was supposed to, Dan, but a clergyman, and I figured that...

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:24.410
Oh, great, Potter, great.

00:16:25.320 --> 00:16:26.300
You figured it.

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:41.030
Oh, Dad, did the film give you any line on the Radcheck killer?

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:44.120
Yeah. He got in and out of the house dressed as a clergyman.

00:16:44.950 --> 00:16:47.200
That's a bad break. Any leads?

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:50.290
Only the telephone call the Radcheck made last night.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:53.040
It's a dial phone, you know. It's pretty tough to trace.

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:56.210
Yeah. I was just about to ask you to come in.

00:16:56.270 --> 00:16:58.610
I'd like to have your opinion on something else that's come up.

00:17:00.440 --> 00:17:03.080
- Ask Mr. Grayson to step into my office, please. - Yes, sir.

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:04.640
Scotland Yard, man.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:07.170
This might be in line with your assignment at Lakeview.

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:12.480
- Any luck, Grayson? - Not yet, sir.

00:17:12.740 --> 00:17:15.910
Your handwriting man haven't been able to identify the writing on the shipping label.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.470
I see.

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:21.760
Dan, this is Mr. Philip Grayson, Scotland Yard. Dan O'Hara, special agent.

00:17:21.890 --> 00:17:24.960
- How do you do? How are you? - You got a lot of your territory, aren't you?

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:28.480
Well, the way things are, it's a little difficult to know where one's territory begins or ends.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:29.560
Well, right you are.

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:32.500
Mr. Grayson made a special trip from London with these.

00:17:32.500 --> 00:17:38.610
That's a very nice painting of San Francisco.

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.370
What is this?

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:43.920
Sir John Godd, our foremost authority on atomic research,

00:17:44.020 --> 00:17:47.860
says that the mathematical equation is a formula of the most advanced nature,

00:17:48.140 --> 00:17:50.290
the solution to a problem in nuclear physics.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:51.190
No, thanks.

00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:54.670
Mr. Grayson was flown over here with the hope that we might identify the source.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:56.440
Would you mind outlining it for him?

00:17:56.460 --> 00:17:58.610
Of course, sir. Here you are. Thanks.

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:03.990
For some months, we've had a very dangerous secret agent under surveillance.

00:18:04.050 --> 00:18:08.400
Thursday last, he received a crate shipped to him from San Francisco Express.

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:10.650
In a normal course, we intercepted it.

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:13.930
It contained a painting. That's a photograph of the painting.

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:17.920
Now, we know our man's not the type to be importing art from America for art's sake,

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:20.730
so we sent it to our lab for examination.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:24.330
Under ultraviolet light, this formula cleverly worked in

00:18:24.410 --> 00:18:26.620
with the pigments of the painting became visible.

00:18:26.940 --> 00:18:30.000
That's a photo of the concealed equation.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.460
to the directors of each of our projects in which Atomic Energy is involved.

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:37.400
Beck flew down to Los Angeles to check with Dr. Townsend at the Lakeview project.

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:59.050
- Excuse me. - Read this, gentlemen.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:16.620
- Mr. Hunter, isn't Lakeview one of your top secrets?

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:18.920
- Our Lakeview laboratory is nearing the completion

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:22.810
of one of our most vital objectives of scientific research.

00:19:22.810 --> 00:19:24.930
A combination of our most advanced knowledge

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:27.750
of the use of guided missiles and atomic force.

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:30.000
- You know, this Radchik affair is beginning to shape

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:35.800
up, Mr. Hunter. Colton was murdered by a suspected subversive in Lakeview. From Mr. Grayson here,

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:39.760
we learned that in London, the secret agent received a painting in which was concealed a

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:46.350
mathematical formula, which we have now traced to Lakeview. Put those two facts together. What do

00:19:46.350 --> 00:19:52.150
they suggest? What you've held from the beginning, that Radcheck wouldn't commit murder just to

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:57.010
escape the relatively minor charge of illegal entry. Exactly. And don't forget Colton's last

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.010
words. He'd stumbled on something red hot.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:01.040
that might be coincidental.

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:03.380
I don't think so, sir.

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:05.220
Come in.

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:10.180
How about it gains?

00:20:10.220 --> 00:20:10.600
Any luck?

00:20:10.880 --> 00:20:12.620
By counting the dial clicks on the record,

00:20:12.660 --> 00:20:13.420
we traced the call.

00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:13.720
Well?

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:15.550
You're not going to like this, Dan.

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:17.250
But Radcheck's friend Igor

00:20:17.250 --> 00:20:19.070
took the call to the public pay station.

00:20:20.480 --> 00:20:21.670
That's all we needed.

00:20:22.370 --> 00:20:23.000
Excuse me.

00:20:25.310 --> 00:20:26.010
Did you say Igor?

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:27.680
Yes, Igor.

00:20:28.480 --> 00:20:28.980
That's interesting.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:33.380
Sir, if you'll take your magnifying glass and look at the photograph of the painting,

00:20:33.630 --> 00:20:35.440
you'll see the name of the artist who signed it.

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:37.460
Igor. Igor Braun.

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:46.840
That all ties up, Dan. I think Braun's your man.

00:20:46.940 --> 00:20:48.650
Sure. Sure is my man.

00:20:48.730 --> 00:20:50.130
But where do I find him? Where is he?

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:51.730
May I make a suggestion, sir?

00:20:52.030 --> 00:20:54.120
If you could find the spot where the picture was painted,

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.510
you might find the artist.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:20:59.830
Mr. Grayson.

00:21:01.180 --> 00:21:03.310
- I'm glad you came over. - Thank you.

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:06.110
Mr. Hunter, I'll need six men born and raised in San Francisco.

00:21:06.110 --> 00:21:09.120
- Know every nook and corner of the city. - You've got them.

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:11.820
Send Morgan in here, please.

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:17.500
With photographs of the painting as the only clue,

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:20.740
agents at the Federal Bureau of Investigation

00:21:20.740 --> 00:21:25.820
searched the city for the location shown in the picture painted by Igor Braun.

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:29.350
Well, what do you think?

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:39.700
- That's it, all right.

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:40.980
It's painted from the rear of one of those houses

00:21:40.980 --> 00:21:43.730
on Clay Street, come on.

00:21:43.730 --> 00:21:45.710
- The point from which the painting had been made

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:47.780
was the rear of this building.

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:54.090
Igor Braun occupied a studio apartment on the third floor.

00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:56.280
Because of the international involvement,

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:58.740
Inspector Grayson was given a special assignment

00:21:58.740 --> 00:22:00.000
to work with O'Hara on the case.

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:03.420
O'Hara set up a complete surveillance of broad,

00:22:03.500 --> 00:22:06.880
including an observation post from which his every move could be watched.

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:17.100
- All right, then. - Oh, how are things on Observatory Hill?

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:23.940
- Okay, thanks. - Not bad.

00:22:24.300 --> 00:22:30.000
- Not bad at all. - Yeah, sure.

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:36.890
you think he'd get nervous having us look over his shoulder like this he looks different from

00:22:36.890 --> 00:22:44.490
his photo he does let me take a look oh sure sure he does now he's got his collar on right

00:22:44.490 --> 00:22:50.680
what's he been doing just painting no visitors not yet any mail he got a gas bill and a light

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:55.230
bill this morning gaines checked with us 10 minutes ago no telephone calls in or out

00:22:55.230 --> 00:23:00.000
didn't he go out he went out to breakfast oh and dan uh this time i went

